Description: Valve's native ARM64 Steam client in a 4 KiB page process tree
 Starts Valve's native ARM64 Linux Steam client through `userpages 4k`, so
 Steam, its runtime, Proton, FEX and the games it starts get the 4 KiB pages
 they assume on Aurora's 16 KiB page kernels. Includes Aurora Play, a small
 launcher for the installed games.
 .
 Valve's runtime carries libibus and lsof for x86 only; the ARM64 client
 takes them from the system. Nothing from Valve is shipped in this package.

Package: steam
Architecture: all
Depends:
 aurora-gamemode,
 aurora-steam-native (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3,
 systemd,
 ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: steam-installer, steam-launcher
Description: Steam for Aurora (native ARM64 client)
 `steam` for Aurora on Apple Silicon. The first start installs Valve's native
 ARM64 Linux client for the current user from Valve's CDN, checked against
 Valve's manifest, then starts it in a 4 KiB page process tree. The kernel
 must be booted with user4k=on (the default on Aurora images).
 .
 Games it starts run under GameMode when gamemoded is available; set
 AURORA_STEAM_GAMEMODE=0 in the environment to start them without it.
